{"parentUuid":"efa5ab8c-880c-432a-b377-8ddced27bc57","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6fa20b73-a995-4ae4-b928-344e193a8ce4","agentId":"a062ff6396a691d74","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01K8EW52ckPp8oURpwj2qzu2","type":"tool_result","content":"# OpenEvolve Release Summary\n\n## Key Releases with Notable Features\n\n**v0.2.27** (18 Mar)\n- Island-based evolution distribution fix\n- SEARCH/REPLACE content in diff summaries\n\n**v0.2.26** (28 Jan) - Major updates\n- \"Manual Mode Support: extended visualizer UI\"\n- \"ARC-AGI-2 example + Event-based early stopping\"\n- \"Large codebase support through LLM changes description + TSP example\"\n- Anthropic parameters bug: \"Fix Anthropic models error when both temperature and top_p\"\n- Configurable snapshot artifacts limit\n\n**v0.2.25** (23 Dec)\n- \"Refactor: Simplify Config.from_dict with dacite and integrate pre-commit\"\n- Circle example updates\n\n**v0.2.24** (18 Dec)\n- Environment variable API key support: \"${VAR} for API key configuration\"\n- \"Fix island population counting per child program\"\n\n**v0.2.23** (11 Dec)\n- \"Make max_tasks_per_child configurable to fix CUDA memory leaks\"\n- SLDBench addition\n\n**v0.2.18** (13 Oct)\n- Novelty rejection sampling feature\n\n## Features NOT Found in Release Notes\n\nThe following requested features are **not mentioned** in the provided release notes:\n- Deterministic seed configuration\n- Circle packing example using Gemini-Flash-2.0 + Claude-3.7-Sonnet ensemble"}]},"uuid":"c8cefb1a-76c6-4c95-8428-56b15aaf61a4","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:50:22.479Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"efa5ab8c-880c-432a-b377-8ddced27bc57","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"cbf66950-4720-4fda-b70c-3ef86ac55b07","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6fa20b73-a995-4ae4-b928-344e193a8ce4","agentId":"a062ff6396a691d74","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KbrJ4kmN1FWQ5wUqj3gNzQ","type":"tool_result","content":"Based on the provided documentation, **DeepSeek V3 pricing is not listed**. The page only shows pricing for two current models:\n\n- **deepseek-v4-flash**: $0.14 per million input tokens (cache miss) and $0.28 per million output tokens\n- **deepseek-v4-pro**: $0.435 per million input tokens (cache miss, with 75% discount) and $0.87 per million output tokens\n\nThe $0.27/$1.10 pricing you mentioned does not appear in this documentation. It's possible that V3 has been deprecated or superseded by the V4 models listed here."}]},"uuid":"050bcde9-7392-4903-b193-d05b936d092e","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:50:22.442Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"cbf66950-4720-4fda-b70c-3ef86ac55b07","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"bc2dc9d6-5287-44ec-a5f7-3fbe901378db","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6fa20b73-a995-4ae4-b928-344e193a8ce4","agentId":"a062ff6396a691d74","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XLjQcuiwKDZsQUzi5BCnwZ","type":"tool_result","content":"REDIRECT DETECTED: The URL redirects to a different host.\n\nOriginal URL: https://www.anthropic.com/pricing\nRedirect URL: https://claude.com/pricing\nStatus: 301 Moved Permanently\n\nTo complete your request, I need to fetch content from the redirected URL. Please use WebFetch again with these parameters:\n- url: \"https://claude.com/pricing\"\n- prompt: \"What is the current pricing per million tokens for Claude Opus 4.7 (or latest Opus) and Claude Sonnet (latest)? Specifically check if Opus is $5/$25 per million tokens or if it's higher (e.g. $15/$75).\""}]},"uuid":"cb2d82e9-4cb7-4e53-9743-d86f0aa2ffd0","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:50:22.671Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"bc2dc9d6-5287-44ec-a5f7-3fbe901378db","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"cb2d82e9-4cb7-4e53-9743-d86f0aa2ffd0","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a062ff6396a691d74","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01JqdyHvHuZtUcPmBYsMKgbE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XD9iCCN1h79vWBUDVtkvGL","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"LLM-LNS ICML 2025 spotlight large neighborhood search Gurobi SCIP"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":27841,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":27841,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CastebPPenCPBXBeiceKe","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"cecef267-6796-4419-864c-91c525f17180","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:50:22.866Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"4b39411e-a86d-439e-8fac-8649623f7c86","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6fa20b73-a995-4ae4-b928-344e193a8ce4","agentId":"a062ff6396a691d74","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VW33pr6LJWksJpU5RPrfPY","type":"tool_result","content":"# AlphaEvolve Paper Details\n\n**Title:** \"AlphaEvolve: A coding agent for scientific and algorithmic discovery\"\n\n**Authors:** Alexander Novikov, Ngân Vũ, Marvin Eisenberger, Emilien Dupont, Po-Sen Huang, Adam Zsolt Wagner, Sergey Shirobokov, Borislav Kozlovskii, Francisco J. R. Ruiz, Abbas Mehrabian, M. Pawan Kumar, Abigail See, Swarat Chaudhuri, George Holland, Alex Davies, Sebastian Nowozin, Pushmeet Kohli, and Matej Balog\n\n**Submission Date:** June 16, 2025\n\n**Abstract Summary:** The paper introduces an evolutionary coding agent that enhances LLM capabilities on challenging scientific and computational tasks. The system iteratively improves algorithms through code changes guided by evaluator feedback. Notable achievements include developing more efficient data center scheduling algorithms, hardware accelerator optimizations, and discovering a matrix multiplication method for 4×4 complex matrices using 48 scalar multiplications—\"the first improvement, after 56 years, over Strassen's algorithm.\"\n\n**Regarding DeepMind:** While this appears to be research involving Google infrastructure optimization, the paper doesn't explicitly identify it as a DeepMind product. The work involves multiple authors and institutions, suggesting collaborative research rather than attribution to a single organization."}]},"uuid":"b45024f8-0334-49da-b58f-8c217ea9a652","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:50:24.182Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4b39411e-a86d-439e-8fac-8649623f7c86","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"5e4dd9ae-8a1b-439c-bdfc-adc02549c64c","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6fa20b73-a995-4ae4-b928-344e193a8ce4","agentId":"a062ff6396a691d74","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01J3FbbKF7YoFW9tWE3Pyt1u","type":"tool_result","content":"# Gemini 2.5 Flash Pricing\n\nYes, that pricing is correct for the standard tier. According to the pricing page:\n\n**Standard tier (paid):**\n- Input: \"$0.30 (text / image / video)\" per million tokens\n- Output: \"$2.50\" per million tokens (including thinking tokens)\n\nThe free tier offers both input and output at no charge, while batch and flex processing modes provide 50% discounts at \"$0.15\" input and \"$1.25\" output respectively."}]},"uuid":"ebdc7f19-ca61-4621-a944-4e67ce13e34f","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:50:27.159Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5e4dd9ae-8a1b-439c-bdfc-adc02549c64c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"cecef267-6796-4419-864c-91c525f17180","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6fa20b73-a995-4ae4-b928-344e193a8ce4","agentId":"a062ff6396a691d74","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XD9iCCN1h79vWBUDVtkvGL","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"LLM-LNS ICML 2025 spotlight large neighborhood search Gurobi SCIP\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"ICML Poster Large Language Model-driven Large Neighborhood Search for Large-Scale MILP Problems\",\"url\":\"https://icml.cc/virtual/2025/poster/43770\"},{\"title\":\"Large Language Model-driven Large Neighborhood Search for Large-Scale MILP Problems | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/forum?id=teUg2pMrF0\"},{\"title\":\"VARIABLE COUPLING-ENHANCED LARGE NEIGHBORHOOD SEARCH FOR SOLVING INTEGER LINEAR PROGRAMS | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/forum?id=AE3jd3Ro0w\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - dongjinkun/COPZoo: Neural Combinatorial Optimization · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/dongjinkun/COPZoo\"},{\"title\":\"SAMPLING-ENHANCED LARGE NEIGHBORHOOD SEARCH ...\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/pdf/83f4455ef873fa935ea9cdaabe668f9ae8fd373d.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"ICML 2025 2025 Spotlight Posters\",\"url\":\"https://icml.cc/virtual/2025/events/2025SpotlightPosters\"},{\"title\":\"Sampling-Enhanced Large Neighborhood Search for Solving Integer Linear Programs | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/forum?id=75MUsbVyWw\"},{\"title\":\"SPL-LNS: Sampling-Enhanced Large Neighborhood Search for Solving Integer Linear Programs\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2508.16171v1\"},{\"title\":\"G-LNS: Generative Large Neighborhood Search for LLM- ...\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2602.08253\"},{\"title\":\"Large neighborhood search and hyper-heuristics for the capacitated p-median problem - PMC\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12832582/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about LLM-LNS at ICML 2025:\n\n## LLM-LNS: ICML 2025 Spotlight Paper\n\nLLM-LNS is a 2025 Spotlight Poster at ICML for \"Large Language Model-driven Large Neighborhood Search for Large-Scale MILP Problems\".\n\n### Overview\n\nThe research proposes LLM-LNS, a novel Large Language Model (LLM)-driven LNS framework for large-scale MILP problems that introduces a dual-layer self-evolutionary LLM agent to automate neighborhood selection, discovering effective strategies with scant small-scale training data that generalize well to large-scale MILPs.\n\n### Key Technical Approach\n\nThe inner layer evolves heuristic strategies to ensure convergence, while the outer layer evolves evolutionary prompt strategies to maintain diversity.\n\n### Performance Results\n\nThe full LLM-LNS framework surpasses manually designed LNS algorithms like ACP, ML-based LNS methods like CL-LNS, and large-scale solvers such as Gurobi and SCIP. It also achieves superior performance compared to advanced ML-based MILP optimization frameworks like GNN&GBDT and Light-MILPopt.\n\nThe paper represents a significant advancement in using LLMs to automate the difficult process of selecting search neighborhoods in optimization problems, with demonstrated improvements over both traditional commercial solvers and other machine learning approaches.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"f7597a79-83bb-4de6-9a89-ee4db10a5119","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:50:29.993Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"cecef267-6796-4419-864c-91c525f17180","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
