{"parentUuid":"7dcf2eec-a00a-4d0e-bb40-2b46012e89c2","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6fa20b73-a995-4ae4-b928-344e193a8ce4","agentId":"a062ff6396a691d74","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EPRQKsMHRQ8EHBrV919mRk","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"AlphaEvolve arXiv 2506.13131 DeepMind Google authors\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"[2506.13131] AlphaEvolve: A coding agent for scientific and algorithmic discovery\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.13131\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - google-deepmind/alphaevolve_results · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaevolve_results\"},{\"title\":\"alphaevolve_results/README.md at main · google-deepmind/alphaevolve_results\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaevolve_results/blob/main/README.md\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) AlphaEvolve: A coding agent for scientific and algorithmic discovery\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/392736011_AlphaEvolve_A_coding_agent_for_scientific_and_algorithmic_discovery\"},{\"title\":\"[PDF] AlphaEvolve: A coding agent for scientific and algorithmic discovery | Semantic Scholar\",\"url\":\"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/AlphaEvolve:-A-coding-agent-for-scientific-and-Novikov-V%CB%9Cu/ed32e5bb11a9e5e2f03ea805782e8670a6e10efd\"},{\"title\":\"AlphaEvolve: A coding agent for scientific and algorithmic discovery\",\"url\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/deepmind-media/DeepMind.com/Blog/alphaevolve-a-gemini-powered-coding-agent-for-designing-advanced-algorithms/AlphaEvolve.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"[2506.13131v1] AlphaEvolve: A coding agent for scientific and algorithmic discovery\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.13131v1\"},{\"title\":\"Paper page - AlphaEvolve: A coding agent for scientific and algorithmic discovery\",\"url\":\"https://huggingface.co/papers/2506.13131\"},{\"title\":\"Autonomous Discovery of Novel Compiler Optimization ...\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2601.21096\"},{\"title\":\"AlphaEvolve: A Gemini-powered coding agent for designing advanced algorithms — Google DeepMind\",\"url\":\"https://deepmind.google/blog/alphaevolve-a-gemini-powered-coding-agent-for-designing-advanced-algorithms/\"}]\n\n## Search Results for AlphaEvolve arXiv 2506.13131\n\nI found comprehensive information about the AlphaEvolve paper from DeepMind/Google. Here's what the search revealed:\n\n### Paper Overview\nAlphaEvolve is an evolutionary coding agent that substantially enhances capabilities of state-of-the-art LLMs on highly challenging tasks such as tackling open scientific problems or optimizing critical pieces of computational infrastructure.\n\n### How It Works\nAlphaEvolve orchestrates an autonomous pipeline of LLMs, whose task is to improve an algorithm by making direct changes to the code. Using an evolutionary approach, continuously receiving feedback from one or more evaluators, AlphaEvolve iteratively improves the algorithm, potentially leading to new scientific and practical discoveries.\n\n### Authors\nThe paper authors are Alexander Novikov, Ngân Vũ, Marvin Eisenberger, Emilien Dupont, Po-Sen Huang, Adam Zsolt Wagner, Sergey Shirobokov, Borislav Kozlovskii, Francisco J. R. Ruiz, Abbas Mehrabian, M. Pawan Kumar, Abigail See, Swarat Chaudhuri, George Holland, Alex Davies, Sebastian Nowozin, Pushmeet Kohli, and Matej Balog. All authors are affiliated with Google DeepMind.\n\n### Key Achievements\n- AlphaEvolve developed a search algorithm that found a procedure to multiply two 4×4 complex-valued matrices using 48 scalar multiplications; offering the first improvement, after 56 years, over Strassen's algorithm in this setting.\n- When applied to optimizing critical components of large-scale computational stacks at Google, AlphaEvolve developed a more efficient scheduling algorithm for data centers, found a functionally equivalent simplification in the circuit design of hardware accelerators, and accelerated the training of the LLM underpinning AlphaEvolve itself.\n\n### Models Used\nAlphaEvolve employs an ensemble of large language models, specifically a combination of Gemini 2.0 Flash and Gemini 2.0 Pro.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"043d096d-10d5-4dd8-8d23-8fe453bfa6eb","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:51:03.182Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7dcf2eec-a00a-4d0e-bb40-2b46012e89c2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"043d096d-10d5-4dd8-8d23-8fe453bfa6eb","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a062ff6396a691d74","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01HDXQmP32ynYB9tv7nTrsN1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All claims verified. Compiling audit results.\n\n## 9 条 claim audit 结果\n\n| # | claim | verdict | 备注 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | OpenEvolve v0.2.27 release 2026-03-18，late beta | **CONFIRMED** | PyPI 实测：v0.2.27 = 2026-03-18 精确匹配 |\n| 2 | 5 个迭代版本 + 4 个功能落地 | **PARTIALLY** | v0.2.23-0.2.27 五个版本全部存在；dacite (0.2.25)、env-var API (0.2.24)、CUDA 内存 (0.2.23)、event-based early stopping (0.2.26) 4 项 release notes 全部 confirmed；**\"确定性 seed\" 在 release notes 找不到，agent 这条夸大** |\n| 3 | OpenAI-compatible + Anthropic bug fix in v0.2.26 + circle packing 用 Gemini-Flash-2.0 + Claude-3.7-Sonnet ensemble 拿 SOTA | **PARTIALLY** | Anthropic temperature/top_p bug fix in v0.2.26 confirmed；**circle packing 双模型 ensemble 在 release notes 中找不到具体描述**，agent 可能从 example 代码推断 |\n| 4 | TSP example v0.2.26 加 large-codebase 模式 | **CONFIRMED** | \"Large codebase support through LLM changes description + TSP example\" 0.2.26 release notes 原文 |\n| 5 | AlphaEvolve arXiv 2506.13131 (2025-06) DeepMind | **CONFIRMED** | 标题 \"AlphaEvolve: A coding agent for scientific and algorithmic discovery\"，submission 2025-06-16，全部作者 Google DeepMind affiliation，github.com/google-deepmind/alphaevolve_results 官方仓库存在 |\n| 6 | DeepSeek V3 $0.27/$1.10 per M tok，500 iter ≈ $5 | **REFUTED** | 官方 pricing page 已经下架 V3，只列 V4-flash ($0.14/$0.28) 和 V4-pro ($0.435/$0.87)；agent 这个数字是过期价 |\n| 7 | Claude Opus 4.7 $5/$25 per M tok | **CONFIRMED** | 多源 (finout / cloudzero / openrouter / pricepertoken) 一致 $5/$25；caveat: 新 tokenizer 同样文本可多消耗 35% token |\n| 8 | Gemini 2.5 Flash $0.30/$2.50 per M tok | **CONFIRMED** | Google 官方 pricing 页 input $0.30 / output $2.50（含 thinking token）原数 |\n| 9 | LLM-LNS ICML 2025 spotlight，打过 Gurobi/SCIP + GNN&GBDT | **CONFIRMED** | ICML 2025 Spotlight Poster (icml.cc/virtual/2025/poster/43770)，OpenReview 摘要原文：\"surpasses... ACP, ML-based LNS methods like CL-LNS, and large-scale solvers such as Gurobi and SCIP. It also achieves superior performance compared to advanced ML-based MILP optimization frameworks like GNN&GBDT and Light-MILPopt\" |\n\n## 关键修正\n\n- **Claim 6 价格过期**：DeepSeek V3 已被 V4 系列取代。V4-flash $0.14/$0.28 比 V3 还便宜（agent 引的是旧价），V4-pro $0.435/$0.87 略贵。500 iter 实际成本：用 V4-flash ≈ $2-3，用 V4-pro ≈ $5-8，**比 agent 报的 $5 还低**（不是变贵）\n- **Claim 2 \"确定性 seed\" 无证据**：release notes 0.2.23-0.2.27 没找到 seed-related entry，可能是 agent 从其他 commit 推断或幻觉\n- **Claim 3 双模型 ensemble**：bug fix 真存在，但\"circle packing 直接用 ensemble 拿 SOTA\" agent 可能合并了不同来源描述\n- **AlphaEvolve 实际用的是 Gemini 2.0 Flash + Gemini 2.0 Pro**（非 Claude），如果项目要复刻 AlphaEvolve 设定，主线应该用 Gemini 双档而不是 Claude+Gemini 混搭\n\n## 路线图修订建议\n\n- **P2 #14 工时 2-3 day claim**：仍有效。OpenEvolve v0.2.27 + dacite config + env-var API + TSP large-codebase mode 三件套使 PoC 起步成本确实降到 2-3 day\n- **API 成本 $5-50/500 iter**：仍有效，可能更便宜。DeepSeek V4-flash 把下限拉到 $2-3，Gemini 2.5 Flash 上限 $10-15\n- **立即可做 verdict**：维持。v0.2.27 release-quality + AlphaEvolve paper + LLM-LNS spotlight 三个独立信号支持\"工程化已成熟\"\n\n## verdict\n\n**PARTIALLY** — 9 条中 5 条 CONFIRMED，3 条 PARTIALLY（细节夸大但主旨对），1 条 REFUTED（DeepSeek V3 已被 V4 取代）。Agent 报告**主线方向可信**（OpenEvolve 成熟、AlphaEvolve paper 真实、LLM-LNS spotlight 真实、工时缩短 reasonable），但**具体 release-notes 细节有润色**（确定性 seed、ensemble 描述）和**API 价格已过时**（DeepSeek V3 → V4）。R13 比 R5/R11 准确度高，但仍需 source-verify 细节才能进 commit-level decision。\n\nSources:\n- [OpenEvolve PyPI](https://pypi.org/project/openevolve/)\n- [OpenEvolve GitHub Releases](https://github.com/codelion/openevolve/releases)\n- [AlphaEvolve arXiv 2506.13131](https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.13131)\n- [google-deepmind/alphaevolve_results](https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaevolve_results)\n- [DeepSeek API Pricing](https://api-docs.deepseek.com/quick_start/pricing)\n- [Gemini API Pricing](https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/pricing)\n- [Claude Opus 4.7 Pricing (finout)](https://www.finout.io/blog/claude-opus-4.7-pricing-the-real-cost-story-behind-the-unchanged-price-tag)\n- [LLM-LNS ICML 2025 Spotlight Poster](https://icml.cc/virtual/2025/poster/43770)\n- [LLM-LNS OpenReview](https://openreview.net/forum?id=teUg2pMrF0)"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1797,"cache_read_input_tokens":36483,"output_tokens":2440,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1797},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":2440,"cache_read_input_tokens":36483,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1797,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1797,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CastijQhcxLHJhHv9YKfC","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"f94c55c9-5f6e-4a18-8223-6b510a31885d","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:51:44.601Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
